<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Haitham bin Tariq</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1954">1954</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Haitham bin Tariq Al Said</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Haitham bin Tariq is the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oman">Oman</a>, who succeeded his cousin <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qaboos-bin-said">Qaboos bin Said</a> in January 2020. Before his accession he served as a senior diplomat, minister of heritage and culture and head of the Oman Vision 2040 committee. As sultan he introduced fiscal reforms, including a value-added tax, and established the position of crown prince for his son.</p></div>
